  "result": "Perfect! All 167 tests pass (143 + 24 new date tests). Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Created src/dates.js with three utilities:**\n\n- `isValidDate(text)` \u2014 validates YYYY-MM-DD format strings\n  - Returns false for non-strings, invalid formats, and non-existent dates\n  - Properly handles leap years (accepts 2024-02-29, rejects 2026-02-29)\n  - Uses UTC validation\n\n- `addDays(date, n)` \u2014 adds/subtracts days to a date\n  - Works in UTC (never local timezone)\n  - Correctly handles month and year boundaries\n  - Negative numbers subtract days\n  - Returns YYYY-MM-DD string\n\n- `daysBetween(a, b)` \u2014 calculates days between two dates (b - a)\n  - Returns whole days in UTC\n  - Negative when b is earlier than a\n  - Consistent with addDays: `daysBetween(a, addDays(a, n)) === n`\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- Imported `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Removed local `isValidDate` function\n- createInvoice now uses the centralized dates module\n\n**Added 24 comprehensive tests to test/dates.test.js:**\n- Valid/invalid date format tests\n- Leap year handling\n- Month and year boundary crossing\n- Negative day additions\n- Consistency between addDays and daysBetween\n- Large date spans\n- Zero-day scenarios\n\nAll date handling is now centralized and consistently works in UTC, ensuring no timezone-related bugs from local machine time.",
